{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing dwellinghouse.<br></p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development shall achieve Secured by design certification to the satisfaction of the local authority &amp;amp; Metropolitan Police, details of which shall be provided to the Local Planning Authority for its written approval prior to the first occupation of the approved development. All security measures applied to the approved development shall be permanently retained thereafter.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Notwithstanding the provisions of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no development falling within Classes A, B, C, D and E in Part 1 of Schedule 2 to that Order shall be carried out without the prior written permission of the Local Planning Authority.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;No part of the property shall be occupied or used\r\nuntil the cycle storage arrangements have been implemented in accordance with\r\nthe approved details. The cycle storage arrangements shall thereafter be\r\nretained&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;Sub-SubTitle&quot;&gt;Adequate\r\nrefuse storage must be provided for both dwelling. This must be shown within\r\nthe plans. The council&#x27;s refuse department should be consulted regarding the design of refuse\r\narrangement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;The\r\napplicant should explore the provision of a new or shared dropped kerb\r\narrangement so that both the host dwelling and the proposed unit benefit from\r\ndedicated off-street parking. Any such arrangement must be agreed in\r\nconsultation with the LBBD Highways Team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;In circumstances where adequate off-street parking cannot be achieved,\r\nthe applicant will be required to submit a parking stress survey, undertaken in\r\naccordance with the Lambeth on-street parking survey methodology. This survey\r\nmust be carried out by an independent company approved by the highways officers\r\nand should provide robust evidence of parking stress levels in nearby streets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Location &amp;amp; Block Plan - drawing no.PL-01 - dated 03.10.2025&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Proposed Site, Floor &amp;amp; Roof Plan - drawing no.PL-04 - dated 03.10.2025&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Proposed Elevations - drawing no.PL-05 - dated 03.10.2025&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design and Access Statement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sustainability Statement&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Biodiversity Exemption Statement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;No other drawings or documents apply.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
